Why This Matters
The OpenShift Virtualization Operator is the foundation for running virtual machines alongside containers in OpenShift. This capability enables:

Hybrid workload management: Run both VMs and containers on the same platform
Legacy application modernization: Gradually migrate traditional VMs to cloud-native architectures
Resource optimization: Better utilize cluster resources by mixing workload types
Simplified operations: Manage VMs using the same tools and processes as containers
